/// Milking sessions in a day (PRD §10.2). Which sessions are active is a farm
/// setting; all four are supported by the data model.
enum MilkSession {
  MORNING
  NOON
  EVENING
  NIGHT
}

/// Business-meaning classification of a milk-log entry (RAKHAL-277). Distinct from
/// `MilkTankType` (which physical tank the milk goes into) — `disposition` is *why*,
/// `tankType` is *where*. Computed by `MilkService` before every insert (never a
/// schema default — see `MilkLogEntry.disposition`'s doc comment): `WITHHELD` for a
/// cow under an active safety withdrawal, `COLOSTRUM` for a cow inside her farm's
/// configured colostrum window since `Lactation.startDate`, `SALEABLE` otherwise.
/// `CALF_FEED`/`DISCARDED`/`HOUSEHOLD_USE` are manual/operator dispositions the
/// schema supports but this ticket's derivation does not assign automatically.
enum MilkDisposition {
  SALEABLE
  WITHHELD
  COLOSTRUM
  CALF_FEED
  DISCARDED
  HOUSEHOLD_USE
}
